# The particle manager's master particle systems drawn by DCLF (CS_DCLF_MASTER_PARTICLES=1, dclf-roadmap.md 1.4): torches, braziers,
# candles and street mist, against master-particles-0.env. Whiterun at night (torches and braziers along the streets), then
# Dragonsreach (candles, braziers), a shot in each; the stats and set parity report every 300 frames.
# In the log: "[DCLF] master particles: on (CS_DCLF_MASTER_PARTICLES, default on)" at startup with "is the engine's" (no FLAG); the report's
# "master particles ... listed" above 0, "left with no event ... <- OK", "held past removal ... <- OK", and the particles' engine passes
# line "<- OK" (no "<- PARTICLES"). Compare the torch flames and the candle flames in the shots with master-particles-0.env's.
CS_DCLF_MASTER_PARTICLES=1
CS_DCLF_STATS=1
CS_DCLF_SET_PARITY=1
DXVK_DEBUG=hang
VK_LOADER_LAYERS_DISABLE=*nsight*
CS_DCLF_TEST_COMMANDS=300:set gamehour to 22;310:set timescale to 0;320:coc Whiterun;1500:dclf:shot=whiterun-night;1600:coc WhiterunDragonsreach;2500:dclf:shot=dragonsreach
CS_DCLF_TEST_EXIT=2600
